Shared agent-hosting infrastructure, not itself revenue-seeking.

An Ansible playbook that provisions a box to run headless coding agents
against this portfolio's own repositories. It exists to increase the
portfolio's engineering throughput, not to be sold, so it has no customers,
no MRR, and nothing for the portfolio router to allocate profit-seeking
effort to.

The top-level README already records this deliberate call. This file makes it
machine-readable so `portfolio/router/validate.py` skips the directory rather
than failing CI on a missing VENTURE.yaml.

Whether this belongs under `ventures/` or under `platform/` is still the open
structural question the README flags; this marker does not settle it.
